      "title": "Public engagements open in August",
      "summary": "The City of Mississauga regularly connects with residents throughout the year to gather their ideas and constructive feedback. This helps guide City plans, programs, services and new developments. Residents and businesses can take part in different ways. You can participate by attending information sessions, open houses and workshops or completing online surveys. The City reviews this feedback along with other data and trends to help decide how to focus its time and resources on community priorities.",
      "url": "https://www.mississauga.ca/city-of-mississauga-news/news/public-engagements-open-in-august/",
      "source": "City of Mississauga",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.mississauga.ca/city-of-mississauga-news/",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-27T12:30:37.000Z"
    },
    {
      "title": "Voting in the 2026 Municipal Election? Check the voters’ list",
      "summary": "Mississauga’s 2026 Municipal Election is on Monday, October 26. Eligible voters will elect Mississauga’s Mayor, their Ward/Regional Councillor and School Board Trustees for the 2026–2030 term of office. Use the Voter Registration Portal to check, update or add your information to the voters’ list before voting begins. Being on the voters’ list helps confirm you’re eligible to vote, helps ensure you receive a Voter notification card and can make the process faster when you arrive to vote.",
      "url": "https://www.mississauga.ca/city-of-mississauga-news/news/voting-in-the-2026-municipal-election-check-the-voters-list/",
      "source": "City of Mississauga",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.mississauga.ca/city-of-mississauga-news/",
